%description:

Tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize:evicts -- the cookie of the second server replaced that of the first.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, client: the number of servers whose Fast Open state is kept
...; a new server then replaces an arbitrary entry; at least 1".

The classes: ample (1024, the default: more servers than the test uses), evicts (a value below
the number of servers: a new server replaces an entry), invalid (below 1). The code:
Tcp::setFastOpenCookie() removes an arbitrary entry when the cache is full; Tcp::initialize()
checks the value. This test separates "evicts" from "ample".

Host under test: host1, a Fast Open client (precondition), on TapSwitchNetwork with two Fast Open
servers, peer[0] and peer[1]. host1 gets a cookie of peer[0] at 0.1 s and one of peer[1] at
0.3 s, and at 0.5 s opens a connection to peer[0] with Fast Open and sends 500 bytes. Observation: level 1, the SYN of connection 3 requests a cookie again and carries no data.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize
%# class: evicts
%# value: 1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenCookieCacheSizeEvicts")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("peer[0]"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN to peer[0]")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.3).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("peer[1]"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN to peer[1]")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[2]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("peer[0]"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 3, to peer[0], with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "" && !matchesExpression(context.event.packet, "pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength");
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 3: a cookie request, without data")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenCookieCacheSizeEvicts compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.fastopenCookieCacheSize = 1    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapSwitchNetwork
*.numPeers = 2
*.peer[*].numApps = 1
*.peer[*].app[0].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.peer[*].app[0].localPort = 1000
*.peer[*].app[0].echoFactor = 0
*.peer[*].tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 3
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenCookieCacheSizeEvicts: PASS
